-**Rules:** verify specifics match (same TGID/supplier/time horizon) before connecting a Slack item to a data signal; near-term (0-2D) ≠ long-term availability; permalink timestamps must fall inside the report week; no time/difficulty editorializing; no extra parens around links.
+4. Extract ONLY signal beyond the data, prioritized by **Hero+ CE × revenue-topic** (the CEs and themes the report's buckets flag).
+5. **Emit structured cards** into the snapshot's `market_review_context` array. Each card:
+
+   ```json
+   {
+     "scope": "market" | "ce",
+     "ce_id": "nyc-statue-of-liberty" | null,
+     "ce_name": "Statue of Liberty" | null,
+     "category": "commission_change" | "availability" | "campaign_decision" | "promo_start_end" | "new_launch" | "competitive_intel" | "supply_issue" | "bug" | "strategy",
+     "text": "Walk Niagara commission up to 35% (from 30%); target 1K PAX by Oct 31 to lock the tier through 2027",
+     "source": "slack",
+     "channel": "#mkt-usa",
+     "author": "Brett Franklin",
+     "permalink": "https://headout.slack.com/archives/CNSHDD2H1/p1752...",
+     "timestamp": "2026-07-08T14:32:00Z"
+   }
+   ```
+
+   **Scope rules:**
+   - `"ce"` — the message names a specific CE, TGID, supplier, or campaign. Set `ce_id` to the matching CE's `combined_entity_id` from the snapshot's `ces[]` array. The template routes these into that CE's drawer.
+   - `"market"` — the message is about the market broadly (holiday flouting, portfolio strategy, competitive landscape, market-wide bug). Leave `ce_id: null`. The template routes these to the §2 Market Review panel.
+
+   **Category vocabulary** (closed set — pick the best fit):
+   | Category | Signal type | Example |
+   |----------|-------------|---------|
+   | `commission_change` | TR negotiation result | "Walk Niagara → 35%" |
+   | `availability` | Inventory/supply break | "Country Music HoF unavailable until Sunday" |
+   | `campaign_decision` | Bid pause, flouting, TROAS change | "American Dream — stop bidding" |
+   | `promo_start_end` | Promo launch or expiry | "KSC promo ended → 34% CVR drop" |
+   | `new_launch` | New CE/product signed | "Alaska Wild Lights — 30%, ~10 blimps" |
+   | `competitive_intel` | Competitor move | "Tripster ~$20-30M rev, Cirque via Outbox" |
+   | `supply_issue` | Vendor/ops/content problem | "Kualoa Ranch CVR hit — availability" |
+   | `bug` | Technical issue impacting revenue | "#tf-bugalert: checkout flow broken on X" |
+   | `strategy` | MMP agenda, portfolio plan, scaling plan | "Six Flags affiliate program proposal" |
+
+6. **Inject cards into the snapshot.** After reading all channels, write the cards array into each market's snapshot JSON at `snapshot["market_review_context"]`, then re-render with `render.py`.
+
+**Rules:** verify specifics match (same TGID/supplier/time horizon) before connecting a Slack item to a data signal; `ce_id` must exactly match a `ces[].ce_id` in the snapshot (grep the snapshot if unsure — a wrong `ce_id` silently orphans the card); near-term (0-2D) ≠ long-term availability; permalink timestamps must fall inside the report week; no time/difficulty editorializing; no extra parens around links.
 
 ### S4: QA + deliver
 
-Confirm the HTML opens. Spot-check per market: **§1 week-type verdict** (header) and **§4 buckets** (B1-B4 home rows + cascade). For Italy/Oceania (no reference gate) sanity-check the headline W0 revenue against Omni. Report the HTML path to the user with the Slack digest.
+Confirm the HTML opens. Spot-check per market: **§1 week-type verdict** (header) and **§4 buckets** (B1-B4 home rows + cascade). For Italy/Oceania (no reference gate) sanity-check the headline W0 revenue against Omni. Check that Slack context cards render: market-scoped in §2 Market Review tab, CE-scoped in their CE drawer. Report the HTML path to the user.
 
